smb: client: Clear sensitive stack data in smb1encrypt.c

jira KERNEL-1962
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9
commit-author Thomas Huth <thuth@redhat.com>
commit 2f9af06e30b78ccb6f2708d89793180c29e4feef
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9/2f9af06e.failed

Make sure to not leak signature data via the stack, clear it
with memzero_explicit() before leaving the function.

To avoid that we have to introduce "goto"-cleanup here, we re-arrange
the code a little bit (and drop the commented cifs_dump_mem debug
code that looks like a leftover from very early days).

	Signed-off-by: Thomas Huth <thuth@redhat.com>
	Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
(cherry picked from commit 2f9af06e30b78ccb6f2708d89793180c29e4feef)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/smb/client/smb1encrypt.c
diff --cc fs/smb/client/smb1encrypt.c
index 0828e3e704c5,c9eb68f04e7b..000000000000
--- a/fs/smb/client/smb1encrypt.c
+++ b/fs/smb/client/smb1encrypt.c
@@@ -185,15 -127,13 +186,26 @@@ int cifs_verify_signature(struct smb_rq
  	rc = cifs_calc_signature(rqst, server, what_we_think_sig_should_be);
  	cifs_server_unlock(server);
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	if (rc)
 +		return rc;
 +
 +/*	cifs_dump_mem("what we think it should be: ",
 +		      what_we_think_sig_should_be, 16); */
 +
 +	if (memcmp(server_response_sig, what_we_think_sig_should_be, 8))
 +		return -EACCES;
 +	else
 +		return 0;
++=======
+ 	if (!rc) {
+ 		if (crypto_memneq(server_response_sig,
+ 				  what_we_think_sig_should_be, 8))
+ 			rc = -EACCES;
+ 	}
++>>>>>>> 2f9af06e30b7 (smb: client: Clear sensitive stack data in smb1encrypt.c)
  
+ 	memzero_explicit(what_we_think_sig_should_be,
+ 			 sizeof(what_we_think_sig_should_be));
+ 	return rc;
  }
* Unmerged path fs/smb/client/smb1encrypt.c
